---- wgmma_config_sweep: correctness, before a single timed launch ----
Every row runs at its OWN `guard_shape`: 3x3 CTAs (so a cluster on EITHER axis spans real peers AND
rounds an odd tile count up to a pad CTA -- a shape one tile wide on an arm's own axis makes its
multicast a copy to self and proves nothing), ktiles = stages+1 for one producer wrap, and ragged M
AND N AND K. TWO arms: exact integers at `==` (a multicast defect is silently wrong data on half the
accumulator rows (A arm) or half its columns (B arm), and an exact verdict localises it to a lane),
and pseudorandom operands against an independent f64 reference at c*sqrt(K)*eps*sum|a*b|, run twice
and demanded bit-identical -- because the exact arm is invariant under ANY reassociation and is
therefore blind to every scheduler change waves 3-5 will make. A fast wrong kernel must not post a timing.
